{"authored" [{"question" "q-161495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nis defined over the type I region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2},\\,-2\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+xy}.\n$$\n\nUse $[a,b]$ as the full nonempty projection of the exactly specified region $R$ onto the $y$ axis. The inner limits may be piecewise. What is $a+b?$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161495/review.json" "file_sha256" "8ae0e6f5584b180942ab5f52d45a42f108c2d4947b802020b5b5613232a2e8fa" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161495/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "a62693250317f43ce631ef430682c2376e7b4caef6f310ef69315ed358ee8dd6" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161495/verification.json" "basis" 2021 "rationale" "Retain original R exactly, require its full actual nonempty projection, enforce ordered fibers, and distinguish source printed interval/accepted key from study mathematics. q161496 projection [1,8/3], answer11/3; q161495 projection[-2,4], answer2 with cap split at-1."} {"question" "q-161495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The inequalities defining $R$ are retained exactly. For every $y\\in[-2,4]$, choosing $x=0$ leaves the nonempty fiber $0\\le z\\le1$. Thus the full nonempty $y$ projection is $[a,b]=[-2,4]$ and $a+b=2$.\n\nThe base must also satisfy $1+xy\\ge0$. When $y<0$, this requires $x\\le-1/y$. The bounds $y^2$ and $-1/y$ meet at $y=-1$. Hence\n\n$$\\iiint_R f\\,dV=\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\int_0^{-1/y}\\int_0^{1+xy}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy+\\int_{-1}^4\\int_0^{y^2}\\int_0^{1+xy}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy.$$\n\nOn the first branch the $x$ cap is $-1/y$; on the second it is $y^2$. The source solution used $x\\le y^2$ throughout and therefore included reversed $z$ bounds for some negative $y$. Its isolated expression $1+xz$ is also a transcription error: the upper $z$ bound is $1+xy$. These solution errors do not change the correct endpoint sum $2$." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161495/review.json" "file_sha256" "8ae0e6f5584b180942ab5f52d45a42f108c2d4947b802020b5b5613232a2e8fa" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161495/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "a62693250317f43ce631ef430682c2376e7b4caef6f310ef69315ed358ee8dd6" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161495/verification.json" "basis" 2021 "rationale" "Retain original R exactly, require its full actual nonempty projection, enforce ordered fibers, and distinguish source printed interval/accepted key from study mathematics. q161496 projection [1,8/3], answer11/3; q161495 projection[-2,4], answer2 with cap split at-1."} {"question" "q-161495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161495/review.json" "file_sha256" "8ae0e6f5584b180942ab5f52d45a42f108c2d4947b802020b5b5613232a2e8fa" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161495/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "a62693250317f43ce631ef430682c2376e7b4caef6f310ef69315ed358ee8dd6" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161495/verification.json" "basis" 2021 "rationale" "Retain original R exactly, require its full actual nonempty projection, enforce ordered fibers, and distinguish source printed interval/accepted key from study mathematics. q161496 projection [1,8/3], answer11/3; q161495 projection[-2,4], answer2 with cap split at-1."} {"question" "q-161495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nis defined over the type I region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2},\\,-2\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+xy}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a0c8097a784b55c27406d8ffdb95f891f6b2c43f5ad3aff3c0357fb22ab15f0" "basis" 2019 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type I region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,y)\\le z\\le {u}_{2}(x,y)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type I region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/1bd4b6d0b1aa955921c1f7855d3fbd95417072a67504d9de9be44dfbbed592e5.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type I region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,y)}^{{u}_{2}(x,y)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,y)=0,\\,{u}_{2}(x,y)=1+xy.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+xy}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2},\\,-2\\le y\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA & ={\\int }_{-2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+xy}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dx\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1+xy}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=-2+4=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a0c8097a784b55c27406d8ffdb95f891f6b2c43f5ad3aff3c0357fb22ab15f0" "basis" 2019 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "986d45b074d202621525e2f4d579743e1ed7e1f54a93934fb99f31c5b0e63474" "basis" 2019 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a0c8097a784b55c27406d8ffdb95f891f6b2c43f5ad3aff3c0357fb22ab15f0" "basis" 2019 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+xy"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/